  "note": "塞外酒肆、酒肆后屋 (native:guanbei/inn_hall, inn_back; 关北 A): a mud-walled hall so low the beams can be touched, the hearth sunk in its middle with the black pot steaming over it, low tables and benches, the keeper's counter and chopping block along the east wall, skins and whips on the walls, the waiting on the bench by the west wall with their untouched bowls; the back room north with the fodder bales, the wine vats, a whole sheep hanging and the keeper's felt bed. Old and used: grease on the floor round the hearth, smoke-black on the beams, straw in the corners.",
